    2. Choose a frame pattern type (lattice with 2xN tile, diamond ring, corner-only, or similar sparse symmetric shape) with bbox 4-7 rows x 4-7 cols.
    3. Place a small inner cluster (2-4 pixels) strictly inside the frame bbox.
    4. Build the output by applying the diagonal-only fill rule to get new inner-color pixels.
    5. Verify output fg has >=1 margin from all grid edges; if not, shift pattern inward.
    6. The input is just the grid before the fill rule was applied (frame + inner on bg).
